            <div xml:id="d999">

                <pb facs="1035" n="915" xml:id="pg915"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">823.00 Revolutions/184: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Peru</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Dearing</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Lima</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-03-17T20:00:00-05:00">March 17, 1931—8
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received March 18—12:09 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>127. New Foreign Minister informs diplomatic corps he will receive its members
                    March 18, 6 p.m. Since Embassy is carrying on with present authorities Embassy
                    staff will attend unless Department perceives some objection.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dearing</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
